ntdll: the x64 register state in the log when an ARM64EC process dies of an unhandled exception.

When no handler takes an exception raised in emulated x64 code, Wine's Unix side prints one line ("Unhandled
exception code c0000005 flags 0 addr 0x1447f3c7d", or "Exception frame is not in stack limits => unable to
dispatch exception") and terminates the process. The line names the instruction, nothing else: not the address
the instruction touched, not where the stack pointer stood, not what the registers held. The debugger Wine starts
instead (winedbg --auto) attaches to a 25 GB, 125-thread process too slowly to say anything before the process is
gone, and a WINEDEBUG=+seh trace, which does print the state at every exception, costs Microsoft Flight
Simulator 2024 two to three times its loading time (it single-steps its own code 57,000 to 225,000 times per boot).

The second-chance NtRaiseException is the last point where the exception still carries an x64 context (the
ARM64EC wrapper converts it to an ARM64 one for the Unix side). On the second chance, when the context is an x64
one, print the exception code, flags, address and the first two parameters, then rip, rsp, rbp, eflags and the
general registers, with the TEB's stack bounds and a note when rsp lies outside them (a thread running on a
coroutine stack whose switch did not update the TIB, which is why the frame was refused). Nothing is printed on a
first chance, so handled exceptions cost nothing. The loading crash of MSFS 2024 on the arm64 line (about one
boot in sixteen, varied sites, three of them a thread resuming with a wrong RSP) is what this is for.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -893,6 +893,24 @@
 {
     ARM64_NT_CONTEXT arm_ctx;
 
+    /* Highball: on the second chance the process is about to die of this exception unless a debugger takes it; the
+     * Unix side prints one line without the state. Print the x64 state here, where it still is an x64 context, so a
+     * crash log says where the thread stood (the TEB stack bounds tell a coroutine stack from a thread's). */
+    if (!first_chance && (context->ContextFlags & CONTEXT_AMD64) == CONTEXT_AMD64)
+    {
+        NT_TIB *tib = &NtCurrentTeb()->Tib;
+
+        ERR( "unhandled x64 exception %08lx flags %lx addr %p info0=%016I64x info1=%016I64x\n",
+             rec->ExceptionCode, rec->ExceptionFlags, rec->ExceptionAddress,
+             (ULONG64)rec->ExceptionInformation[0], (ULONG64)rec->ExceptionInformation[1] );
+        ERR( " rip=%016I64x rsp=%016I64x rbp=%016I64x eflags=%08lx stack=%p-%p%s\n",
+             context->Rip, context->Rsp, context->Rbp, context->EFlags, tib->StackLimit, tib->StackBase,
+             (context->Rsp < (ULONG64)tib->StackLimit || context->Rsp > (ULONG64)tib->StackBase) ? " (rsp outside the TEB stack)" : "" );
+        ERR( " rax=%016I64x rbx=%016I64x rcx=%016I64x rdx=%016I64x\n", context->Rax, context->Rbx, context->Rcx, context->Rdx );
+        ERR( " rsi=%016I64x rdi=%016I64x  r8=%016I64x  r9=%016I64x\n", context->Rsi, context->Rdi, context->R8, context->R9 );
+        ERR( " r10=%016I64x r11=%016I64x r12=%016I64x r13=%016I64x\n", context->R10, context->R11, context->R12, context->R13 );
+        ERR( " r14=%016I64x r15=%016I64x mxcsr=%08lx\n", context->R14, context->R15, context->MxCsr );
+    }
     context_x64_to_arm_xstate( &arm_ctx, (ARM64EC_NT_CONTEXT *)context );
     /* a debugger reads and sets the thread's debug registers at the event through the context the server keeps for
      * it, which only brings back what it carries; one captured by native code (RtlRaiseException) has none yet */
